The `kubectl` skill confirms that a strategic merge patch is the correct approach to change a specific container's command without altering other parts of the deployment spec.

The target deployment is `app` in namespace `default`.
The container is named `app`.
The old command is defined by the list: `sh`, `-c`, `exit 1`.
The new command should be: `sleep 3600` (or similar).

I will construct the patch using strategic merge patch.

Patch definition:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "command": ["sh", "-c", "sleep 3600"]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
I will apply this patch and then verify the rollout and replica count.

